•        With wheels/pull handle - PN 1205522, PN 1205520 (with thermometer)
•        With side handles - PN 1205523, PN 1205521 (with thermometer)";s:14:"specifications";s:991:"{"format":"andison_specs_v3","text":"","tables":[{"tableHtml":"<table><thead><tr><th>Voltage</th><th>100-240 Volts - Single phase</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Temperature</td><td>100°F - 300°F Adjustable</td></tr><tr><td>Heating element</td><td>300 watts</td></tr><tr><td>Thermostat</td><td>Adjustable with indicator light</td></tr><tr><td>Thermometer</td><td>Optional digital thermometer</td></tr><tr><td>Insulation</td><td>Fiberglass batt (1.50 inches)</td></tr><tr><td>Chamber depth</td><td>20.00 inches</td></tr><tr><td>Chamber diameter</td><td>8.00 inches</td></tr></tbody></table>","tableMatrix":{"mode":"standard","headers":["Voltage","100-240 Volts - Single phase"],"rows":[["Temperature","100°F - 300°F Adjustable"],["Heating element","300 watts"],["Thermostat","Adjustable with indicator light"],["Thermometer","Optional digital thermometer"],["Insulation","Fiberglass batt (1.50 inches)"],["Chamber depth","20.00 inches"],["Chamber diameter","8.00 inches"]],"merges":[]}}]}";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:115:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/type_5_pic_1_20260407_083212_0.jpg";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-07T06:32:15.292033+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:2:{i:0;s:115:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/type_5_pic_1_20260407_083212_0.jpg";i:1;s:115:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/type_5_pic_2_20260407_083213_1.jpg";}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:8:"Gal Gage";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:5:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14366;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:15:"measuring-gauge";s:5:"brand";s:8:"Gal Gage";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"Cat No. 1";s:5:"model";s:19:"Hi-Lo Welding Gauge";s:4:"type";s:29:"Welding Measuring Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:702:"The G.A.L. Gage Cat No. 1 Hi-Lo Welding Gauge is a multi-purpose inspection tool used primarily for pipe and weld fit-up, measuring in both standard (inches) and metric (millimeters) scales. It is made of stainless steel and helps to reduce radiographic rejects. 

Features
Material: Premium stainless steel construction.
Scale: Dual measurement system (inches on one side, millimeters on the other).
Design: Slim, lightweight design (approx. 30% lighter than older models).
Operation: Manual operation with an adjustable locking mechanism (locking screw) to hold measurements for reference.
Compliance: Helps satisfy fit-up codes for organizations such as ASME, ANSI, API, and Military standards.";s:14:"specifications";s:775:"Key Specifications and Measurement Capabilities
The Cat No. 1 gauge can perform up to six different measurement functions: 
•        Internal Misalignment: Measures the internal mismatch of pipe wall alignment before and after tacking, which helps to cut down on radiographic rejects.
•        Fit-up Gap: Measures the required gap after fit-up, specifically between 1/16" and 3/32".
•        Material/Pipe Wall Thickness: Assesses the material or pipe wall thickness.
•        Fillet Weld Leg Length: Checks the leg length of a fillet weld.
•        Butt Weld Reinforcement (Crown Height): Measures the crown height or reinforcement of a butt weld.
•        Bevel Angle Verification: Includes go/no-go features to verify a common beveled angle of 37-1/2 degrees.";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:44:01.640252+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:1;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14367;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:15:"measuring-gauge";s:5:"brand";s:8:"Gal Gage";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"Cat No. 2";s:5:"model";s:34:"Single Purpose Hi-Lo Welding Gauge";s:4:"type";s:29:"Welding Measuring Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:803:"The G.A.L. Gage Cat No. 2 is a Single Purpose Hi-Lo Welding Gauge primarily used to measure internal misalignment (high-low) and root weld space in pipe or plate welding, checking fit-up gaps from 1/32" up to 3/16" (or 1/16" to 3/32" range for the economy model) with stainless steel construction for durability. It features both inch and metric scales, engraved markings for easy reading, and is available in economy (Cat #2) or professional (Cat #2 Pro) versions, with the Pro offering a specific tolerance of ±0.006" for accuracy in the 1/32" to 3/16" range. 

How it Works (for Fit-up):
You insert the gauge's alignment stops into the gap; if the thin part doesn't fit, the gap is smaller; if it goes through, it's larger, helping you determine if the fit-up meets code requirements before welding.";s:14:"specifications";s:497:"Key Specifications & Features:
•        Function: Measures internal misalignment (Hi-Lo) and root weld gap.
•        Material: Stainless Steel, deburred for safety.
•        Measurement Scale: Dual Inch/Metric.
•        Range (Economy): Checks fit-up gaps (approx. 1/16" to 3/32").
•        Range (Pro): For gaps between 1/32" and 3/16".
•        Tolerance (Pro): ±0.006".
•        Markings: Engraved for clarity.
•        Versions: Economy (Cat #2) and Professional (Cat #2 Pro).";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:44:01.640252+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:2;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14368;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:15:"measuring-gauge";s:5:"brand";s:8:"Gal Gage";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"Cat No. 4";s:5:"model";s:16:"Bridge Cam Gauge";s:4:"type";s:29:"Welding Measuring Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:833:"The G.A.L. Gage Cat No. 4 Bridge Cam Gauge is a versatile welding inspection tool used to measure various aspects of a weld in both inches and millimeters. 

Measurement Capabilities
The Cat No. 4 gauge can perform up to seven different types of measurements on welded surfaces and joints: 
•        Angle of preparation: Measures angles from 0° to 60°.
•        Excess weld metal (capping size): Also known as weld reinforcement.
•        Depth of undercut: Measures the depth of grooves next to the weld.
•        Depth of pitting: Measures the depth of small depressions.
•        Fillet weld throat dimension: Measures the distance from the joint root to the weld face.
•        Fillet weld leg length: Measures the leg length of the weld.
•        Misalignment (high-low): Measures the offset of plates or pipes.";s:14:"specifications";s:29:"see specs table Gal Gage.docx";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:44:01.640252+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:3;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14369;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:15:"measuring-gauge";s:5:"brand";s:8:"Gal Gage";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"Cat No. 6";s:5:"model";s:34:"Automatic Weld Size AWS Type Gauge";s:4:"type";s:29:"Welding Measuring Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:758:"The G.A.L. Gage Cat No. 6 (GAL-6) Automatic Weld Size AWS Type Gauge is a pocket-sized, stainless-steel tool used for the inspection and calibration of butt and fillet welds. It is designed for precise measurement of various weld features. 

Measurement Functions
The gauge is used to check the following aspects of a weld: 
•        Fillet Weld Leg Size: Determines the actual leg length of the weld.
•        Fillet Weld Throat Size: Checks the throat dimension against specifications.
•        Weld Reinforcement: Measures the excess weld metal (capping size) on butt welds.
•        Convexity & Concavity: Verifies the permissible tolerances for the profile of fillet welds.
•        Undercut/Pits: Can check permissible tolerance of underfill.";s:14:"specifications";s:446:"Key Specifications
•        Manufacturer: G.A.L. Gage Company
•        Part Number: GAL-6 (Inch version) or GAL-6-M (Metric version)
•        Material: Stainless Steel
•        Measurement Range: Up to 3/4" (0" - 0.75") for the inch version
•        Dimensions: Approx. 3.5 x 3.5 x 0.6 inches (8.89 x 8.89 x 1.52 cm)
•        Functions: Measures actual fillet weld leg length, permissible convexity, concavity, and weld reinforcement.";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:44:01.640252+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:4;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14370;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:15:"measuring-gauge";s:5:"brand";s:8:"Gal Gage";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"Cat No. 8";s:5:"model";s:29:"7-piece fillet weld gauge set";s:4:"type";s:29:"Welding Measuring Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:259:"The G.A.L. Gage Cat No. 8 is a 7-piece fillet weld gauge set used for the inspection of concave or convex fillet welds. It allows for fast and accurate measurement of eleven different fillet weld sizes, ranging from 1/8 inch to 1 inch (or metric equivalents).";s:14:"specifications";s:694:"Key Specifications
•        Function: Measures fillet weld leg size and throat size to determine if they meet specifications.
•        Measurement Range: 1/8", 3/16", 1/4", 5/16", 3/8", 7/16", 1/2", 5/8", 3/4", 7/8", and 1". Metric versions cover 3.175 mm to 25.4 mm.
•        Material: Each blade is made from 1/4" x 4" cold-rolled stainless steel to resist rust and bending.
•        Markings: All sizes and numerals are laser engraved into the surface to prevent rubbing off.
•        Portability: The set of seven blades comes in a handy pocket case and weighs only about 4 ounces (0.26 lbs).
•        Installation Method: Designed for use with arc-welding installation methods.";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:44:01.640252+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:8:"Garryson";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:1:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:16646;s:11:"category_id";s:11:"power-tools";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:11:"accessories";s:5:"brand";s:8:"Garryson";s:12:"product_name";s:0:"";s:5:"model";s:22:"Tungsten Carbide Burrs";s:4:"type";s:22:"Power Tool Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:633:"Garryson Tungsten Carbide Burrs are manufactured from premium-grade tungsten carbide to deliver high cutting efficiency, long tool life, and consistent performance. Designed for high-speed applications, these burrs provide excellent resistance to wear, heat, and chipping. Available in a wide range of shapes, sizes, and cut styles, they are suitable for precision grinding, profiling, deburring, edge preparation, and weld removal. Compatible with pneumatic and electric die grinders, Garryson carbide burrs are engineered for use on hardened steel, stainless steel, cast iron, aluminum, and other ferrous and non-ferrous materials.";s:14:"specifications";s:0:"";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:120:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/carbide_burrs_-_1_20260407_074722_0.jpg";s:10:"created_at";s:31:"2026-04-07T05:47:26.45773+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:2:{i:0;s:120:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/carbide_burrs_-_1_20260407_074722_0.jpg";i:1;s:120:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/carbide_burrs_-_2_20260407_074723_1.jpg";}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:10:"HARDWORKER";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:1:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:16779;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:27:"