Time saving of spatter removal. Extremely easy spatter removal from inside, outside and nozzle end";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"Length : 210 mm
Weight : 280 g
Made in Japan";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:116:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/mo-zero.8_-_0_20260407_090358_0.jpg";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-07T07:04:03.161585+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";s:11:"accessories";s:6:"images";a:6:{i:0;s:116:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/mo-zero.8_-_0_20260407_090358_0.jpg";i:1;s:116:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/mo-zero.8_-_1_20260407_090359_1.jpg";i:2;s:116:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/mo-zero.8_-_2_20260407_090359_2.jpg";i:3;s:116:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/mo-zero.8_-_3_20260407_090400_3.jpg";i:4;s:116:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/mo-zero.8_-_4_20260407_090400_4.jpg";i:5;s:116:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/mo-zero.8_-_5_20260407_090401_5.jpg";}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:7:"Kobelco";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:1:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14340;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-consumables";s:14:"subcategory_id";N;s:5:"brand";s:7:"Kobelco";s:12:"product_name";s:27:"Familiarc/Trustarc/Premiarc";s:5:"model";s:35:"Welding Electrodes and Filler Wires";s:4:"type";s:19:"Welding Consumables";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:1196:"For over 50 years, KOBELCO is the preferred brand of welding consumables in Japan & Southeast Asia. As a world class global manufacturer. KOBELCO is well positioned to meet the demanding welding needs of various industries worldwide.

FAMILIARC : Consumables used for general welded structures made of mild steels & high tensile steels that have tensile strength of less than 590Mpa.

TRUSTARC : Consumables used for steels that require tensile strength of 570Mpa & higher, low temperature steels & heat-resistant alloy steels.

PREMIARC : Consumables used for high-alloy steels, stainless steels & non-ferrous metals like in hardfacing, for cast iron and nickel-based alloy.

APPLICATIONS : 

Process
•        Stick Electrode (SMAW)
•        Flux Cored Wire (FCAW)
•        Saw Flux and Wire Combination (SAW)
•        Solid Wire (GMAW)
•        TIG Welding Rod and Wire GTAW)

Steel Type
•        Hard facing 
•        Heat Resistant Steel
•        Mild Steel and 490MPa High Tensile Strength Steel
•        Weatherproof Steel
•        High Tensile Steel and Low Temperature Steel
•        Stainless Steel
•        Cast Iron
•        9% Ni Steel and Nickel-Based Alloy";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:49.057466+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:9:"MAGNAFLUX";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:7:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14345;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:31:"non-destructive-crack-detection";s:5:"brand";s:9:"Magnaflux";s:12:"product_name";s:5:"SKC-S";s:5:"model";s:35:"Spotcheck Cleaner / Remover Aerosol";s:4:"type";s:27:"Liquid Penetrant Inspection";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:476:"SKC-S is an NDT-approved solvent cleaner/remover for pre-cleaning before non-destructive testing and for removing excess surface penetrant from an inspection area before applying developer during liquid penetrant testing.

This non-halogenated solvent remover can be used on a wide range of substrates to remove oils, greases and other contaminants. SKC-S dries quickly without leaving a residue, and meets the low-residue requirements for NDT and aerospace penetrant testing.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:52.844701+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:1;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14346;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:31:"non-destructive-crack-detection";s:5:"brand";s:9:"Magnaflux";s:12:"product_name";s:6:"SKD-S2";s:5:"model";s:27:"Spotcheck Developer Aerosol";s:4:"type";s:27:"Liquid Penetrant Inspection";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:568:"A bright white, non-aqueous developer, SKD-S2 creates an opaque white background for high-contrast penetrant testing and quickly draws penetrant out to create stronger, clearer indications for better inspection reliability and sensitivity.

Noted for its compatibility with special alloys, such as stainless steel, aluminum, magnesium and titanium, SKD-S2 is non-halogenated, can be used with Type 1 & Type 2 penetrants. This solvent-based developer meets aerospace and nuclear industry requirements, and complies with all major NDT specifications, including ISO 3452.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:52.844701+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:2;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14347;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:31:"non-destructive-crack-detection";s:5:"brand";s:9:"Magnaflux";s:12:"product_name";s:7:"SKL-SP2";s:5:"model";s:27:"Spotcheck Penetrant Aerosol";s:4:"type";s:27:"Liquid Penetrant Inspection";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:612:"SKL-SP2 is a solvent removable penetrant for portability, especially for welding operations, and is post emulsifiable for greater resolution of flaw indications. It produces a visible red color contrast, and features outstanding penetrating characteristics. SKL-SP2 is highly reliable at locating surface open flaws and discontinuities and can be used on non-porous ceramics and similar materials. Typically used on welds, forgings, pressure vessels, castings, general metal work, leak testing, and in power plants and construction applications.

SKL-SP2 is listed on the QPL SAE AMS 2644 Qualified Product List.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:52.844701+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:3;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14348;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:31:"non-destructive-crack-detection";s:5:"brand";s:9:"Magnaflux";s:12:"product_name";s:5:"WCP-2";s:5:"model";s:29:"Magnavis White Contrast Paint";s:4:"type";s:28:"Magnetic Particle inspection";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:575:"A bright white, opaque NDT contrast paint, WCP-2 provides a high contrast background to improve probability of detection and sensitivity during visible magnetic particle inspections.

This fast drying paint aerosol sprays on evenly, without flaking, before inspection so when nonfluorescent / colored magnetic particles are applied, the indications appear clearly against the opaque white background.

WCP-2 can be used with all types of colored and visible mag particles, including 7HF and 7C Black wet method particles, or #2 Yellow and #8A Red dry method magnetic powders.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:52.844701+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:4;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14349;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:31:"non-destructive-crack-detection";s:5:"brand";s:9:"Magnaflux";s:12:"product_name";s:3:"7HF";s:5:"model";s:52:"Magnavis Prepared Bath Black Magnetic Ink Wet Method";s:4:"type";s:28:"Magnetic Particle inspection";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:657:"A highly-sensitive oil-based magnetic particle aerosol for non-fluorescent (visible) wet method magnetic particle testing to locate fine and medium discontinuities on finished parts.

7HF provides clear, strong indications due to the heavy buildup of the highly magnetic particles. The convenient aerosol packaging is ideal for field testing, spot inspections and places where bulk processing
is impractical, and the wide spray pattern makes it easy to cover large areas for faster processing during remote inspections of tubing, piping and large structures.

7HF is often used with WCP-2 white contrast paint to improve contrast and inspection sensitivity.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:52.844701+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:5;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14350;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:31:"non-destructive-crack-detection";s:5:"brand";s:9:"Magnaflux";s:12:"product_name";s:4:"14HF";s:5:"model";s:33:"Magnaglo Flourescent Magnetic Ink";s:4:"type";s:28:"Magnetic Particle inspection";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:430:"MAGNAGLO® 14HF is an oil-based, ready-to-use fluorescent ink for wet method magnetic particle testing. It gives clear bright yellow/green indications when viewed in a darkened area under UV(A) of peak avelength 365nm.

Used in conjunction with suitable magnetising equipment, 14HF will locate medium-fine surface and slightly sub-surface defects. 14HF is widely regarded as the test material of choice for aerospace applications.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:52.844701+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:6;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14351;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:31:"non-destructive-crack-detection";s:5:"brand";s:9:"Magnaflux";s:12:"product_name";s:3:"Y-1";s:5:"model";s:16:"AC Magnetic Yoke";s:4:"type";s:28:"Magnetic Particle inspection";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:633:"The Y-1 is an AC electromagnetic yoke and the new generation of light weight, ergonomically designed yokes that improve job performance and productivity by reducing operator arm and wrist fatigue when testing in tight, confined and overhead areas. Provides a portable means of creating AC magnetic fields for the detection of surface indications during magnetic particle testing.

Lightweight, less than five pounds, and ergonomic with a molded grip and trigger on/off switch, the Y-1 has impact and chemical-resistant construction. Includes a robust strain-relieved ten-foot cord and carrying grommet for convenience in field use.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:52.844701+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:6:"Makita";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:7:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:16137;s:11:"category_id";s:11:"power-tools";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:7:"grinder";s:5:"brand";s:6:"Makita";s:12:"product_name";s:5:"9553B";s:5:"model";s:35:"4” 710W Heavy Duty, Angle Grinder";s:4:"type";s:11:"Power Tools";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:296:"Product Highlights
•        Compact yet powerful grinder. Small body grip for easy handling.
•        Motor with high heat-resistance performance. Dust proof construction.
