•        EGX technology";s:14:"specifications";s:640:"{"format":"andison_specs_v2","text":"","tableMatrix":{"mode":"grouped-pairs","leadColumns":0,"headers":["PABMA","JIS","VOLTS","ENDURO","EXCEL","GOLD","L","W","H"],"groups":[{"title":"TYPE","span":2,"rowSpan":false},{"title":"VOLTS","span":1,"rowSpan":true},{"title":"AMPERES","span":3,"rowSpan":false},{"title":"DIMENSIONS (mm)","span":3,"rowSpan":false}],"rows":[["B20","NS40","12","","","35","196","128","198"],["1SN","NS60","12","42","50","45","230","138","210"],["1SM","NS50","12","50","65","65","233","173","205"],["2SM","N50","12","69","68","65","258","171","202"],["3SM","N70","12","70","80","75","306","171","202"]],"rowMerges":[]}}";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:108:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/excel_20260407_034132_0.png";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-07T01:43:35.199241+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:1:{i:0;s:108:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/excel_20260407_034132_0.png";}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:5;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:15734;s:11:"category_id";s:9:"batteries";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:17:"special-batteries";s:5:"brand";s:8:"MOTOLITE";s:12:"product_name";s:12:"Solar Master";s:5:"model";s:24:"Deep-Cycle Solar Battery";s:4:"type";s:9:"Batteries";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:322:"The Solar Master, Motolite's dedicated deep-cycle solar battery, is designed for solar installations and other applications that require minimal maintenance. It's loaded with all the deep-cycle battery features you could possibly need: long life, low discharge rate, long discharge period and excellent cycling capability.";s:14:"specifications";s:0:"";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:115:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/solar_master_20260407_034332_0.png";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-07T01:43:35.199241+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:1:{i:0;s:115:"https://ldsvzhzgyfewwprizrok.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/solar_master_20260407_034332_0.png";}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:17:"Panasonic Connect";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:31:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14781;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:19:"tig-welding-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:12:"YC-300BP4YAA";s:5:"model";s:78:"Full Digital (Inverter) Controlled 300 Amps.  AC/DC TIG Welding Machine 220VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:654:"The Panasonic BP4 Series is a full-digital AC/DC TIG welding power source engineered for high-quality, versatile aluminum and steel welding across a wide range of plate thicknesses and joint types. With advanced inverter control, flexible arc performance, and an intuitive touch panel with Welding Navigation, it makes setup simple—even for less experienced operators. Pulse functions, expert modes, and precise frequency control help deliver stable arcs, smooth bead quality, and excellent penetration in both TIG and manual welding processes. The BP4 Series combines powerful performance with ease of use for professional industrial TIG applications.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:1;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14782;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:22:"plasma-cutting-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:12:"YP-060PF3YAA";s:5:"model";s:84:"Full Digital (Inverter) Controlled 60 Amps. Air Cooled Plasma Cutting Machine 220VAC";s:4:"type";s:22:"Plasma Cutting Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:589:"The Panasonic PF3 Series is a high-performance air plasma cutting system designed for precision and efficiency. Featuring full digital control, it delivers cleaner, more uniform cuts and extends consumable life for reduced operating costs. The intuitive control panel and standard Cutting Navigation make setting the optimal current simple for any user. In addition to high-quality cutting, select models support air plasma gouging and can be integrated with robotic systems for enhanced automation and accuracy. Ideal for applications requiring reliable, high-quality cutting performance.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:2;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14783;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:22:"plasma-cutting-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:12:"YP-080PF3YAA";s:5:"model";s:84:"Full Digital (Inverter) Controlled 80 Amps. Air Cooled Plasma Cutting Machine 220VAC";s:4:"type";s:22:"Plasma Cutting Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:589:"The Panasonic PF3 Series is a high-performance air plasma cutting system designed for precision and efficiency. Featuring full digital control, it delivers cleaner, more uniform cuts and extends consumable life for reduced operating costs. The intuitive control panel and standard Cutting Navigation make setting the optimal current simple for any user. In addition to high-quality cutting, select models support air plasma gouging and can be integrated with robotic systems for enhanced automation and accuracy. Ideal for applications requiring reliable, high-quality cutting performance.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:3;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14784;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:22:"plasma-cutting-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:12:"YP-130PF1YAA";s:5:"model";s:82:"Inverter Controlled 130 Amps Water Cooled Plasma Cutting Machine YP-130PF1  220VAC";s:4:"type";s:22:"Plasma Cutting Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:601:"The Panasonic YP-130PF1 is a robust inverter air plasma cutting system engineered for high-efficiency cutting of thick metal plates up to 70 mm with exceptional precision. Equipped with a water-cooled design and capable of continuous 100 % duty-cycle operation, it’s ideal for demanding industrial applications and extended cutting tasks. The unit also features a built-in coolant tank, air regulator, and torch monitor for easier maintenance and reliable performance. With compatibility for robot integration, this machine delivers precise, high-speed cutting for automated production environments.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:4;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14792;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:20:"g3-controller-series";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:20:"TM/TL S-AWP WG3/WGH3";s:5:"model";s:52:"Super Active TAWERS Series Arc  Welding Robot System";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:726:"Overview
•        6 Axis Articulated Arc Welding Robot
•        High speed welding and ultra-low spatter over a wider current range
•        Improved productivity at 100 cm/min or higher with beautiful and wide bead
•        Stable weld quality. Stabilizing the arc by changing wire feed speed at constant cycle
•        Larger torch angle window. Super Active TAWERS minimize spatter generation even with steep push / trial torch angle
•        High quality welding of thin material, with exceptionally good penetration
•        High quality CO2 welding. 98% less spatter generation at 200 A 
•        99% spatter reduction by MAG welding at 250 A
•        Input Power : 3-Phase, 200/220VAC, 22kVA, 50/60 Hz";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:5;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14793;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:20:"g4-controller-series";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:15:"TM/TL G4 Series";s:5:"model";s:63:"G4 Series – Arc Welding Robot (Separate Welding Power Source)";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:3:"New";s:11:"description";s:1189:"Overview
•        Designed for flexible integration with an external welding power source (separated type) for optimized system configuration. 
•        Advanced welding control optimization tailored to robot posture for reduced cycle times and improved productivity. 
•        Improved spatter reduction through modern welding methods, contributing to higher-quality welds and less cleanup. 
•        Intuitive teach pendant with touch panel, making operation and programming easier and more efficient. 
•        Eliminates the need for an external step-down transformer at many international sites, simplifying setup and installation. 
•        OPC UA compatibility enables seamless integration with peripheral devices and industrial networks for connected workflows. 
•        Enhances robot motion performance with faster axis speeds and more accurate control for smoother, efficient welding cycles. 
•        High-resolution touch interface and 3D display, improving visibility and ease of programming even with gloves on. 
•        Open communication standards and connectivity features support integration with sensors, data systems, and automation infrastructure.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:6;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14785;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:27:"accessories-and-consumables";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:11:"Red Torch 4";s:5:"model";s:21:"MAG/MIG Welding Torch";s:4:"type";s:19:"Welding Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:931:"Panasonic offers a variety of MIG/MAG welding torches, available in different amperage ratings and cooling methods to suit various applications. These torches are designed for use with their range of welding machines and are known for their durability and performance. 
Available Models and Specifications 
Panasonic welding torches are primarily categorized by their current rating (amperage) and cooling system (air-cooled or water-cooled). 
•        Pana 200A Series: Air-cooled models suitable for lighter-duty applications, typically running at 100A for mixed gas applications at 100% duty cycle.
•        Pana 350A Series: Air-cooled or water-cooled options designed for more demanding fabrication, providing up to 350A at 100% duty cycle for CO2 welding.
•        Pana 500A Series: Heavy-duty air-cooled or water-cooled torches for high-current applications, capable of handling 500A at 60% duty cycle for CO2 welding.";s:14:"specifications";s:597:"•        Duty Cycle: This is the percentage of time a torch can operate at its maximum rated current within a 10-minute cycle. For example, a 500A torch with a 60% duty cycle can weld at 500A for 6 minutes continuously.
•        Applicable Wire Diameter: Torches support various wire diameters, typically ranging from 0.8 mm to 1.6 mm, depending on the specific model and liner used.
•        Compatibility: Torches are available with different connector types, including the standard Panasonic connector and the common Euro-connector, ensuring versatility across different welding machines.";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";s:17:"welding-torch-gun";s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:7;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14786;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:20:"g3-controller-series";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:14:"TM/TL WG3/WGH3";s:5:"model";s:38:"TAWERS Series Arc Welding Robot System";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:892:"Overview
•        6 Axis Articulated Arc Welding Robot
•        Robot systems with integrated welding power source technology "TAWERS"
Robot system controls the welding waveform directly
•        Continuously evolving by addition of application
Suitable for Multi-material of welding material
•        Weld Navigation Function
•        Welding Process : CO2 / MAG / Stainless steel MIG / Pulse MAG / Stainless Pulse MIG
•        Output Current Range : 30 to 350 A DC (WGIII) / 30 to 450 A DC (WGHIII)
•        Duty Cycle : CV: 80% @ 350 A / Pulse : 60% @ 350 A (WGIII)
                           : 100 % (WGHIII)
•        TAWERS 100 kHz advanced inverter technology makes possible :
o        Low spatter welding
o        Welding with less heat input
o        Thin and thick plate welding
o         A maximum flexibility
o        Reduce production cost
o        Improve quality";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:8;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14800;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:30:"featured-products-and-solution";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:4:"VRPS";s:5:"model";s:31:"Virtual Robot Progamming System";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:3:"New";s:11:"description";s:782:"Overview
Panasonic Robot & Welding System Solutions presents the Virtual Robot Programming System (VPRS). This solution enables even unskilled robot operators to execute welding robot programming efficiently. The VRPS uses a digital twin of the welding robot that follows the movements of the manually guided torch model. Movements and welding tasks are defined on the real workpiece with the torch model, the virtual sequence is then transferred to the robot controller to be repeated by the robot. Two key benefits render the VPRS a great tool to improve your production:

• robot operators do not require years of experience, knowledge, or skill to program the robot

• the robot programming time is reduced drastically by simply using virtual reality on the actual workpiece";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:9;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14801;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:30:"featured-products-and-solution";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:4:"iWNB";s:5:"model";s:30:"Integrated Welding Network Box";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:3:"New";s:11:"description";s:1591:"Overview
iWNB by Panasonic is an advanced welding management solution that delivers digitalization, visualization, and real-time oversight of welding robot operations. Designed for smart factories and production lines, it collects and displays key production data to help teams boost productivity, improve quality, and enhance traceability across multi-robot welding cells — all accessible via a web browser. 

Key Features
• Digital Visualization of Welding Data
View current operating status, historical records, and production results for up to 32 robots connected over LAN — all through an intuitive web interface. 
• KPI & OEE Monitoring
Track essential performance indicators including KPIs and Overall Equipment Effectiveness (OEE) to better understand productivity trends and efficiency. 
• Production & Operation Insights
Check real-time production status, average cycle times, cost performance (e.g., energy and consumables per work), and detailed operation histories. 
• Traceability & Error History
Access historical welding results, error lists, and weld line information for improved quality tracking and compliance. 
• Breakdown & Troubleshooting Tools
Identify frequent short stops or long stoppages with breakdown rankings and built-in troubleshooting guidance. 
• Maintenance Support
Monitor robot load factors, feed motor current, and tip wear estimates, with notifications and maintenance history logging. 
• Web-Based Access
No client-side software installation needed — users can securely access the system via standard browsers on company networks.";s:14:"specifications";s:620:"Benefits for Your Production Workflow
•        Increased Productivity: Visualization of production and downtime helps you pinpoint inefficiencies and improve cycle time. 
•        Quality & Traceability: Comprehensive historical recording supports quality assurance and traceability for audits and continuous improvement. 
•        Smarter Decision-Making: Consolidated dashboards and performance metrics help managers make faster, data-driven decisions. 
•        Easy Monitoring: Web application format enables remote access and broad visibility across welding operations without specialized software installs.";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:10;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14772;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:23:"co1-mag-welding-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"YD-350KR2";s:5:"model";s:69:"Thyristor Controlled 350Amps CO2/MAG Welding Machine 220VAC or 440VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:675:"The Panasonic KR2 Series is a line of reliable thyristor-controlled semi-automatic welding power sources designed for CO?/MAG welding applications. These best-selling machines deliver smooth, easily controlled arcs and straightforward current-based setup, making them suitable for both experienced welders and newcomers. Built with a robust, dustproof and waterproof structure for versatility across jobsite conditions, the series includes energy-saving circuits that reduce standby power consumption and enhanced safety features such as short-circuit current limiting and failure detection. Maintenance is simplified with conveniently placed controls and service components.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:11;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14773;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:23:"co1-mag-welding-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"YD-500KR2";s:5:"model";s:70:"Thyristor Controlled 500Amps CO2/MAG Welding Machine  220VAC or 440VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:675:"The Panasonic KR2 Series is a line of reliable thyristor-controlled semi-automatic welding power sources designed for CO?/MAG welding applications. These best-selling machines deliver smooth, easily controlled arcs and straightforward current-based setup, making them suitable for both experienced welders and newcomers. Built with a robust, dustproof and waterproof structure for versatility across jobsite conditions, the series includes energy-saving circuits that reduce standby power consumption and enhanced safety features such as short-circuit current limiting and failure detection. Maintenance is simplified with conveniently placed controls and service components.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:12;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14774;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:23:"co1-mag-welding-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"YD-600KH2";s:5:"model";s:92:"Thyristor Controlled 600 Amps. CO2/MAG/DC Manual/DC GOuging Welding Machine 220VAC or 440VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:289:"Features:
•        Most Suitable for High Current & High Duty Cycle Welding
•        Best Suited for Thick Plate Welding
•        Optional windproof model available
•        Excellent Performance across a wide current range
•        With DC Arc Gouging and DC Stick function";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:13;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14775;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:23:"co1-mag-welding-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"YD-350RX1";s:5:"model";s:60:"Inverter Controlled 350 Amps. CO2/MAG Welding Machine 220VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:727:"The Panasonic RX1 Series (YD-200RX1 / YD-350RX1 / YD-500RX1) is a high-performance inverter-based semi-automatic welding solution designed for CO?/MAG welding applications. Built for energy efficiency and superior welding quality, the RX1 integrates advanced digital waveform control for stable arcs and smooth starts, enhancing overall weld consistency. Its compact, lightweight, and robust design ensures durability across diverse jobsite environments, while a clear digital display and intuitive controls make operation simple and accessible. Detailed settings can be fine-tuned via front-panel switches, and the series maintains compatibility with ancillary devices from Panasonic’s KR2 lineup, easing equipment upgrades.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:14;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14776;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";N;s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"YD-350GR3";s:5:"model";s:90:"Full Digital (Inverter) Controlled 350 Amps. CO2/MAG/Stainless MIG Welding Machine 220 VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:590:"The Panasonic GR3 Series is a full digital CO?/MAG/MIG semi-automatic welding power source engineered for high-quality, stable arc performance in industrial welding applications. Featuring advanced digital control and high-precision encoder feedback, it delivers smooth arc starts, reduced spatter, and consistent wire feeding across a broad current range. The intuitive control panel and compatible remote unit simplify operation, while optional aluminum welding models expand versatility. Reliable and user-friendly, the GR3 Series enhances productivity for professional fabrication work.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:15;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14777;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";N;s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"YD-400VP1";s:5:"model";s:87:"Full Digital (Inverter) Controlled 350 Amps. CO2/Pulsed MAG/MIG Welding Machine 220 VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:518:"The Panasonic VP1 Series is a full-digital CO?/MAG/MIG welding power source designed for high-precision pulse welding and superior aluminum MIG performance. Featuring advanced pulse control for beautiful bead appearance, intuitive digital operation with Welding Navigation, and wide data output for quality management, the VP1 makes setup and control easier even for less experienced users. Built for versatility across materials and welding conditions, it’s ideal for industrial semi-automatic welding applications.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:16;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14778;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:19:"tig-welding-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"YD-300WX4";s:5:"model";s:68:"Twin Inverter Controlled 300 Amps.  AC/DC TIG Welding Machine 220VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:672:"The Panasonic WX4 Series is a high-performance AC/DC TIG welding machine engineered for versatile, precision welding of aluminum, mild steel, and stainless steel. With multiple welding modes—including Panasonic’s proprietary Mix TIG (AC/DC alternating output)—and adjustable pulse frequency, it delivers excellent arc control, smooth bead quality, and adaptability across thin to thick materials. Built with user-friendly features such as easy mode switching, safety functions, 50/60 Hz compatibility, and comprehensive data output for quality control, the WX4 Series is ideal for industrial TIG welding applications that demand reliability and high-quality results.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:17;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14779;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:19:"tig-welding-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:12:"YD-200BL3YNA";s:5:"model";s:74:"Full Digital (Inverter) Controlled 200 Amps. DC TIG Welding Machine 220VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:615:"The Panasonic YC-200BL3 is a compact, lightweight DC TIG welder ideal for on-site and workshop welding tasks. Its full digital control delivers stable, high-quality welds with precise current settings and excellent arc starts. Equipped with DC pulse and arc spot functions, it allows tailored weld profiles and uniform bead appearance. The unit also features memory storage for welding conditions and an easy-to-use control panel, making setup and repeatable performance simple. With a robust yet portable design and included torch and gas regulator, the BL3 is perfect for professional DC TIG welding applications.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:18;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14780;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:19:"tig-welding-machine";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:12:"YD-300BZ3YAA";s:5:"model";s:75:"Full Digital (Inverter) Controlled 300 Amps.  DC TIG Welding Machine 220VAC";s:4:"type";s:15:"Welding Machine";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:549:"The Panasonic YC-300BZ3 is a full digital DC TIG welding power source engineered for stable, high-quality welding performance across a wide range of current settings. Featuring fast arc startup, intuitive LCD controls, and Welding Navigation for easy condition setup, it supports both TIG and manual welding with digital memory for storing multiple welding profiles. Its compact, lightweight design enhances mobility without sacrificing precision, making it ideal for professional DC TIG welding applications in workshop and production environments.";s:14:"specifications";s:46:"see specs table Panasonic Welding Machines.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:19;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14787;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:27:"accessories-and-consumables";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:29:"All New Red Tig Welding Torch";s:5:"model";s:17:"TIG Welding Torch";s:4:"type";s:19:"Welding Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:1074:"Panasonic offers a variety of TIG welding torches with options for both air-cooled and water-cooled systems to accommodate different amperage requirements and duty cycles. These torches are compatible with Panasonic TIG welding machines and can also be used with other machines via common adapters like the Euro-connector. 

Panasonic TIG torches, such as those in the YT series, are available in a range of current ratings and with different cooling methods. 
•        Air-Cooled Torches: These are typically used for lower amperage TIG welding applications, generally up to around 200A. They are more portable and lighter but can become hot during extended high-amperage welding. An example is a 300A (DC) / 210A (AC) rated air-cooled torch, which is rated at a 20% duty cycle.
•        Water-Cooled Torches: Designed for high-amperage and continuous-duty cycles (e.g., 100% duty cycle at 310A or higher), these torches use liquid coolant circulation for superior heat management, leading to better operator comfort and longer consumable life during prolonged welding.";s:14:"specifications";s:581:"•        Rated Current (Amperage): Available from 80A up to 500A, depending on the model and cooling method.
•        Duty Cycle: This is the percentage of time the torch can operate at its maximum current. Water-cooled torches often have a 100% duty cycle, while air-cooled ones might have 20-60%.
•        Applicable Electrode Diameter: Torches support various tungsten electrode diameters, such as 1.6mm, 2.4mm, and 3.2mm.
•        Compatibility: They can be connected to various TIG welding machines, with options for different plugs and cable lengths (e.g., 4m or 8m).";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";s:17:"welding-torch-gun";s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:20;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14788;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";N;s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:29:"Genuine Parts and Consumables";s:5:"model";s:17:"Torch Consumables";s:4:"type";s:19:"Welding Consumables";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:1801:"Panasonic offers a range of consumables for MIG/MAG and TIG welding torches designed for industrial applications. These consumables are replaceable components intended for high-performance use.

Common Consumables by Torch Type
•        MIG/MAG Torches: These torches, such as the Panasonic 200A, 350A, and 500A models, require specific consumables that ensure stable wire feeding and gas coverage.

o        Contact Tips: Guide the welding current to the wire and are available in various diameters (e.g., 0.8mm, 1.0mm, 1.2mm) to match the welding wire size.
o        Gas Nozzles: Direct the shielding gas to the weld puddle and come in different sizes and styles (e.g., conical).
o        Tip Body/Holders: Secure the contact tip in place and facilitate the connection of other parts.
o        Gas Orifice/Diffusers: Help ensure an even flow of shielding gas.
o        Inner Tubes and Liners: A tube that guides the welding wire from the feeder to the torch head; they are available for different current ratings like 200A, 350A, and 500A.
o        Torch Body: The bent tube assembly that holds the consumables and directs the wire and gas.

•        TIG Torches: Consumables for TIG torches (e.g., WP9, WP17, WP26 models) focus on precise control of the arc and shielding gas.

o        Collets and Collet Bodies: Hold the tungsten electrode securely in the torch head.
o        Ceramic Nozzles / Cups: Direct the flow of argon or other shielding gas to the weld area.
o        Gas Lenses: Provide superior gas coverage, which is often preferred for high-quality welds.
o        Tungsten Electrodes: The non-consumable electrode used to create the arc (though they wear down over time).
o        Back Caps (Long/Short): Cover the back of the torch and help hold the electrode assembly in place.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:21;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14789;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:27:"accessories-and-consumables";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:9:"YX-09KGC1";s:5:"model";s:18:"Water Cooling Unit";s:4:"type";s:19:"Welding Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:1510:"The Panasonic YX-09KGC1 is a robust, compact water-cooling unit for MIG/TIG welding systems, designed to protect torches and enhance performance during high-amperage, continuous welding, featuring built-in safety flow switches, quick connectors, and rugged construction for industrial use, ensuring consistent welds and longer torch life. It's part of Panasonic's line of welding accessories, available with various input voltage options, and is essential for maintaining stable, high-quality welding in demanding environments like shipyards, automotive, and railways. 
Key Features & Functions:
•        High Cooling Capacity: Efficiently dissipates heat, preventing torch overheating.
•        Safety: Includes an integrated flow switch to monitor coolant, ensuring reliable protection.
•        Ease of Use: Designed for quick setup with universal quick connectors.
•        Durable & Portable: Features a rugged frame and handles for job site transport.
•        Application: Ideal for high-amperage MIG/TIG welding, protecting torches and improving arc stability.
•        Model Variations: Available in different versions (e.g., YX-09KGC1 for standard, YX-09KGB1 for insulated). 

How it Works:
Coolant Circulation: Circulates cooling liquid (like Coolant G) through the welding torch.
Heat Removal: Carries heat away from the torch head, allowing for higher currents.
Protection: The flow switch detects coolant flow; if it stops, the system shuts down or alerts the user, preventing damage.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";s:11:"accessories";s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:22;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14790;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:27:"accessories-and-consumables";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:8:"YX-25AD1";s:5:"model";s:29:"CO2 Gas Regulator with Heater";s:4:"type";s:19:"Welding Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:233:"The Panasonic CO2/MAG gas regulator that includes a heater and a 2-pin plug, designed for use in semi-automatic welding. It is a reliable, cylinder-mounted unit commonly used with Panasonic welding machines to ensure stable gas flow.";s:14:"specifications";s:740:"Key Specifications
Gas Service: Suitable for both CO2 (Carbon Dioxide) and MAG (Ar80%+CO220% mix) welding.
Maximum Flow Rate: Provides a maximum flow of 25 L/min.
Inlet Connection: Features a W22-14 right-hand female nut for connection to the gas cylinder.
Outlet Connection: Uses an φ8.5mm hose nipple (or 6.5mm depending on the exact variant) for the gas hose.
Heater: This model typically includes a heater, which is a crucial component for CO2 regulators to prevent the gas from freezing in the regulator as it expands.
Welding Compatibility: It is a standard accessory for various Panasonic CO2/MAG/MIG welding machines, ensuring compatibility and stable arc performance when used in appropriate systems.
Weight: Approximately 1.3 kg.";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";s:11:"accessories";s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:23;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14791;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:20:"g3-controller-series";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:15:"TM/TL G3 Series";s:5:"model";s:34:"G3 Series Arc Welding Robot System";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:385:"Overview
•        6 axis articulated arc welding robot
A variety of the selectable features specialized for arc welding
•        Combination with Full Digital welding power source achieves stable and high quality welding
Good bead appearance and low spatter even in high speed welding
•        Manipulator type selectable to fit your application
Arm length / Payload / Torch type";s:14:"specifications";s:416:"•        Input Power : 3-Phase,  200/220VAC,  3kVA, 50/60Hz
•        Memory Capacity : 40,000 points
•        Position Control : Software servo control
•        Control Axes : 6 axes simultaneously (Max. 27 axes)
•        Input and Output : 40 points (Optionally expandable up to 2048 points) 
•        Welding Process, Output current/voltage and Duty Cycle depends on the welding power source capability";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:24;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14794;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:20:"g4-controller-series";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:14:"TM/TL WG4/WGH4";s:5:"model";s:81:"Panasonic TAWERS WG4 – Arc Welding Robot (Welding Power Source Integrated Type)";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:3:"New";s:11:"description";s:1404:"Overview
•        Integrated Welding Power Source (TAWERS): Robot controller and welding power source are fully integrated for seamless control and high-speed data communication, eliminating interface delays and improving welding consistency. 
•        Low Spatter Welding: MTS-CO2 welding method as standard significantly reduces spatter for cleaner welds and less post-weld cleanup. 
•        Advanced Welding Processes: Supports CO2, MAG, MIG and stainless-steel welding applications with precision and reliability. 
•        Enhanced Productivity: Optimized control according to robot posture helps shorten cycle times and boost throughput. 
•        Intuitive Touch Panel Teach Pendant: High-resolution touch interface and 3D display make programming and operation more user-friendly—even with gloves on. 
•        Improved Motion and Control: Faster axis movement and improved motion accuracy help deliver smoother, more efficient welding cycles. 
•        Compact, Space-Saving Design: Cables and components arranged to minimize footprint without sacrificing performance. 
•        Industry Standard Connectivity: Conformance with OPC UA facilitates integration with peripheral devices and supports smart factory workflows. 
•        Functional Safety: Designed to comply with international safety standards, with software-based safety mechanisms for flexible, safer operation.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:25;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14795;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:20:"g4-controller-series";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:19:"TM/TL AWP4 WG4/WGH4";s:5:"model";s:42:"Active TAWERS 4 (AWP4) - Arc Welding Robot";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:3:"New";s:11:"description";s:1522:"Overview
•        AWP4 (Active Wire Process 4) compatibility: Works seamlessly with TAWERS (WG4) to achieve ultra-low spatter and stable arc control during welding.
•        Ultra-low spatter welding: High-precision wire feeding and advanced waveform control dramatically reduce spatter—by up to ~98 % in CO? welding compared to conventional methods—resulting in cleaner welds and less post-weld cleanup. 
•        High-speed welding capability: Optimized arc response enables faster welding speeds without compromising weld quality.
•        Integrated power source control (TAWERS): Direct communication between robot controller and welding power source ensures precise, real-time control for consistent results.
•        Improved bead quality: Enhanced molten puddle stability produces a flatter, higher-quality weld bead surface across a wide range of materials. 
•        Supports multiple shielding gases: Works with CO2, MAG, and MIG gases, making it versatile for various welding applications. 
•        High-duty-cycle capability: The air-cooling torch mechanism enables heavy-duty production with an 80 % duty cycle at 310 A output (CO2 welding), supporting long, continuous operations. 
•        Boosts productivity: By reducing spatter and improving weld quality, AWP4 minimizes rework and enhances overall production efficiency.
•        Suitable for mass-production environments: Ideal for automotive and industrial applications requiring high efficiency and repeatable welding quality.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T03:48:46.851784+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}i:26;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14796;s:11:"category_id";s:18:"arc-welding-robots";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:20:"g4-controller-series";s:5:"brand";s:17:"Panasonic Connect";s:12:"product_name";s:22:"TM/TL-G4/WG4 TIG Robot";s:5:"model";s:24:"TIG Welding Robot System";s:4:"type";s:17:"Arc Welding Robot";s:5:"badge";s:3:"New";s:11:"description";s:809:"Overview
