•        Sintered inlet filter";s:14:"specifications";s:26:"see specs table TANAKA.doc";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:56.481494+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:9:"Technotex";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:1:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14489;s:11:"category_id";s:20:"drilling-and-lifting";s:14:"subcategory_id";N;s:5:"brand";s:9:"Technotex";s:12:"product_name";s:0:"";s:5:"model";s:24:"Polyester Webbing Slings";s:4:"type";s:11:"Nylon Sling";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:1577:"Technotex web slings are heavy-duty synthetic lifting slings, primarily made from polyester or advanced materials like Dyneema, designed for safely lifting extremely heavy loads (up to 180 tons) in demanding industries like oil & gas, mining, and construction, offering lightweight handling, high strength, durability, and compliance with international safety standards like EN 1492-1. Key features include high abrasion resistance, resistance to chemicals/UV, and innovative designs for better safety and efficiency. 

Key Features & Benefits:
•        High Capacity: Can lift loads from 1 ton up to 180 tons, significantly reducing the need for heavy metal slings.
•        Lightweight: Made from synthetic fibers, making them easier and safer for workers to handle than metal alternatives.
•        Durable & Abrasion Resistant: Constructed with premium polyester, often with special treatments or woven structures for enhanced resistance to wear, chemicals, and UV light, extending lifespan.
•        Versatile: Available in flat webbing and round sling designs, suitable for various lifting and rigging applications.
•        Safety Standards: Compliant with international standards (CE, GS, TUV, ISO 9001, EN 1492-1), ensuring reliable performance.
•        Cost-Effective: Reduced replacement frequency and improved handling times lower overall operational costs. 

Applications:
Used across various sectors, including energy, oil & gas, offshore, shipping, and general industry, for tasks requiring safe and efficient lifting of large or sensitive materials";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:44:21.959007+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:10:"Tempilstik";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:1:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14357;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"welding-accessories";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:18:"industrial-markers";s:5:"brand";s:10:"Tempilstik";s:12:"product_name";s:0:"";s:5:"model";s:28:"Temperature Indicating Stick";s:4:"type";s:17:"Industrial Marker";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:1269:"Providing accuracy, confidence and compliance for over 80 years, Tempilstik is the original temperature-indicating stick with the best combination of precision and convenience for surface temperature measurement. Specially engineered for accurate temperature indication in pre-heating, interpass and post-weld heat treating applications, Tempilstik is the industry's leading choice for use in the most critical jobs. 

Features & Benefits :
•        116 temperatures available from 100°F(38°C) to 2000°F(1093°C)
•        Stick instantly melts at designated temperature for easy and immediate visual inspection.
•        Calibration-free with 100% reliability
•        Comply with preheat temperature requirements of AWS D1.1, ASME Code Sec. I, III and VIII, ANSI/ASME Code B31.1 and B31.3.
•        Imprinted part number, temperature and lot code across entire stick for improved traceability
•        Made in U.S.A.

Industry Uses :
•        Welding
•        Ship building
•        Metal fabrication
•        Railroad
•        Fracking
•        Oil & gas production
•        Transmission

Surface Uses :
•        Steel
•        Iron
•        Aluminum
•        Stainless Steel
•        Glass
•        Plastic
•        Ceramic";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:31:"2026-04-06T02:43:57.77078+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";N;s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:9:"Tokin Arc";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:0:{}}s:7:"Truweld";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:1:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14332;s:11:"category_id";s:19:"arc-welding-machine";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:27:"accessories-and-consumables";s:5:"brand";s:7:"Truweld";s:12:"product_name";s:33:"Welding Accessoried & Consumables";s:5:"model";s:25:"Accessories & Consumables";s:4:"type";s:19:"Welding Accessories";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:567:"TruWeld is a Singapore-based manufacturer and supplier of professional welding equipment and accessories, specializing in high-quality TIG, MIG, and plasma welding torches, consumables, tungsten electrodes, and complementary welding components compatible with leading global brands. Trusted since 1993, TruWeld offers extensive inventory, competitive pricing, and fast fulfilment to support fabricators, distributors, and industrial customers locally and around the world — helping enhance productivity and reliability in metal fabrication and welding applications.";s:14:"specifications";s:3:"N/A";s:5:"price";s:0:"";s:5:"image";s:0:"";s:10:"created_at";s:32:"2026-04-06T02:43:40.560765+00:00";s:18:"sub_subcategory_id";s:17:"welding-torch-gun";s:6:"images";a:0:{}s:9:"datasheet";s:0:"";}}}s:4:"UVEX";a:2:{s:11:"description";s:0:"";s:8:"products";a:11:{i:0;a:16:{s:2:"id";i:14421;s:11:"category_id";s:10:"protection";s:14:"subcategory_id";s:14:"eye-protection";s:5:"brand";s:4:"Uvex";s:12:"product_name";s:16:"Supravision I-VO";s:5:"model";s:36:"The "Eye-Volution" in Eye Protection";s:4:"type";s:29:"Personal Protective Equipment";s:5:"badge";s:0:"";s:11:"description";s:1051:"Uvex i-Vo, the “Eye-Volution” in protective eyewear. When it comes to comfort and looks, I-Vo does not compromise, making these spectacles incredibly popular among wearers. Soft components around the sensitive parts of the face (nose, forehead, ears) guarantee permanent maximum comfort.

Features 
•        Comfort and design without compromise
•        Spectacles provide maximum wearer comfort
•        Uvex duo component technology – combines hard and soft components for maximum wearer comfort
•        Soft components around the sensitive parts of the face (ears, forehead, nose)
•        Available with fully adjustable side arms enables the wearer to achieve an individual fit
•        Also available with head strap for working at heights or in confined spaces. Also aids compatibility with other items of PPE.
•        Available Lenses Color:
